<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0" xmlns:itunes="http://www.itunes.com/dtds/podcast-1.0.dtd" xmlns:googleplay="http://www.google.com/schemas/play-podcasts/1.0"><channel><title><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></title><description><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></description><link>https://harryjamescoburn.substack.com</link><image><url>https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!l6zR!,w_256,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7ba3ea74-e261-4cc2-88d9-03901029eedf_1500x1500.jpeg</url><title>Harry James Coburn</title><link>https://harryjamescoburn.substack.com</link></image><generator>Substack</generator><lastBuildDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:30:13 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://harryjamescoburn.substack.com/feed" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><copyright><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></copyright><language><![CDATA[en-gb]]></language><webMaster><![CDATA[harryjamescoburn@substack.com]]></webMaster><itunes:owner><itunes:email><![CDATA[harryjamescoburn@substack.com]]></itunes:email><itunes:name><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></itunes:name></itunes:owner><itunes:author><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></itunes:author><googleplay:owner><![CDATA[harryjamescoburn@substack.com]]></googleplay:owner><googleplay:email><![CDATA[harryjamescoburn@substack.com]]></googleplay:email><googleplay:author><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></googleplay:author><itunes:block><![CDATA[Yes]]></itunes:block><item><title><![CDATA[Fix the bucket before you pour AI into it]]></title><description><![CDATA[Find where your revenue leaks before you automate anything]]></description><link>https://harryjamescoburn.substack.com/p/fix-the-bucket-before-you-pour-ai</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://harryjamescoburn.substack.com/p/fix-the-bucket-before-you-pour-ai</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:00:48 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/47b9aff7-6f5f-4e40-9f69-51ad93ce57d4_1456x816.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Many CEOs want AI in their sales process before they know where their revenue leaks.</p><p>So that's my first question to any CEO: where does yours leak?</p><p>Picture your funnel as a bucket. Leads go in the top, revenue comes out the bottom. On the way there are holes: the wrong customers, a pitch that doesn't land, deals that stall after the demo, a price that gets discounted away.</p><p>Pour AI into a leaky bucket and you get more water on the floor, faster.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png" width="1456" height="1000" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1000,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:119842,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ipn6!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2c17b5c4-1f6b-44a8-8b42-aaa7b142b09c_1456x1000.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h3>Find the leak first</h3><p>Before you automate anything, answer four questions:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Customer:</strong> who actually buys, and who just takes meetings? Pull your last 20 wins and losses and write down what the best fits have in common.</p></li><li><p><strong>Message:</strong> can everyone on the team say in one sentence who you're for and why it matters, in the customer's words?</p></li><li><p><strong>Flow:</strong> where do most deals stall? Write exit criteria for every stage and find the one where deals get stuck.</p></li><li><p><strong>Price:</strong> are you selling on value, or discounting to close?</p></li></ol><h3>Then automate the repetitive work</h3><p>Once you know where the leak is, look at the repetitive tasks around it: researching accounts, enriching leads, routing inbound, first drafts of follow-ups, updating the CRM. That's where AI pays back fast.</p><h3>What it looked like</h3><p>At a forest carbon scale-up I worked with, the biggest gains came from the basics. We focused on the right customers. We split each market into someone who created pipeline and someone who closed (SDRs and AEs). We got the message right on the buyers' real problems and hurdles, and mapped every stakeholder and brought them in early. In the end, those sales were all about trust.</p><p>The average sales cycle went from 75 days to 16.</p><h3>What to do this month</h3><p>Find the one stage where most deals stall. Fix that before you buy another tool.</p><p>Where does your bucket leak most: the customer, the message, the flow or the price? Hit reply and tell me.</p><p>Not sure? The 2-minute scorecard will show you: <a href="https://harryjamescoburn.com/scorecard.html?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=2026-11-12-fix-the-bucket">harryjamescoburn.com/scorecard</a></p><p>HJC</p>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sales still runs on trust]]></title><description><![CDATA[What this newsletter is, who it's for, and what you'll get from it]]></description><link>https://harryjamescoburn.substack.com/p/sales-still-runs-on-trust</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://harryjamescoburn.substack.com/p/sales-still-runs-on-trust</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Harry James Coburn]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 07:01:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c8ecffd2-69aa-4867-8950-78f7ea79c177_1456x816.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Many CEOs are being told AI will fix their sales. Few have been told what to give it, how to teach it, or when to trust it.</p><p>That's what this newsletter is for.</p><p>I've spent my career building sales teams, first in big companies like IBM and Lloyds Banking Group, then in VC-backed start-ups across Europe and the UK. At a forest carbon scale-up, quarterly sales went from about &#8364;0.1M to &#8364;5.4M in nine months (estimated on the company's own model). At an early-stage start-up, I built a B2B business from nothing to 60% of company revenue.</p><p>Neither happened because of a clever tool. We found what worked, proved it small, then scaled it.</p><h3>The formula</h3><p>Every sales team I've worked with comes down to four things:</p><ul><li><p>how many of the right deals you create</p></li><li><p>how fast they close</p></li><li><p>how many you win</p></li><li><p>how much each one is worth</p></li></ul><p>New revenue = deals created &#215; win rate &#215; deal size &#247; time to close.</p><p>Every fix I make moves at least one of them.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png" width="1456" height="1000" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1000,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:120303,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Vhus!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd00b920-f853-4daf-82d7-6eb150290aa9_1456x1000.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h3>Where AI fits</h3><p>AI is now the fastest way to move all four. It can answer every inbound lead in minutes, research accounts, draft follow-ups and keep the CRM clean. At one company I worked with, AI agents got first replies to inbound leads from about a day to five minutes.</p><p>It can also flood buyers with generic messages and burn the trust that wins deals. The biggest mistake I see is using AI to replace the moments that matter, instead of the repetitive work around them.</p><p>So my rule is simple: train AI on your own past deals, test it with real buyers, and only scale it once it sends what you would send, at least 95% of the time.</p><h3>What you'll get</h3><p>Every Thursday, one issue on one of those four things, or one AI workflow:</p><ul><li><p>what's usually going wrong</p></li><li><p>what I'd change this month</p></li><li><p>what happened when a real company did it</p></li></ul><p>Short and practical. Written for CEOs of VC-backed companies, Series A to C, who are launching something new or whose sales stalled after a raise.</p><h3>One question</h3><p>What's stuck in your sales right now? Hit reply and tell me. I read every reply, and the best questions become issues.</p><p>If you'd like to see where your sales are leaking first, my 2-minute scorecard is here: <a href="https://harryjamescoburn.com/scorecard.html?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=2026-11-05-sales-runs-on-trust">harryjamescoburn.com/scorecard</a></p><p>HJC</p>]]></content:encoded></item></channel></rss>